{"id": "lg_elec-2026-11-09-008", "date": "2026-11-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": ["lg_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Jilin OLED files to invalidate an LG Chem OLED material patent in Korea, the first such challenge by a Chinese company", "content": "<p>According to industry sources in Korea, China's <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/jilin-OLED-material-tech\">Jilin OLED Material Tech</a> asked Korea's Intellectual Property Trial and Appeal Board (IPTAB) to invalidate an OLED material patent owned by <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/lg-chem\">LG Chem</a>. This is the first time that a Chinese company has filed an invalidation trial against one of LG Chem's OLED patents in Korea. The request was filed in November 2025, and in late October 20", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/jilin-oled-files-invalidate-lg-chem-oled-material-patent-korea-first-such", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-09-009", "date": "2026-11-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Homways (formerly Metaways) starts production at its second 12-inch OLED microdisplay fab, in Chuzhou", "content": "<p>China-based OLED microdisplay producer <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/metaways\">Homways</a> (previously Metaways) announced that it has started production at its second 12-inch OLED microdisplay (OLEDoS) production line, in Chuzhou, Anhui province. The line, operated by the company's subsidiary Anhui Hongxi Microdisplay Technology, held its production-start ceremony on November 6, 2026.</p><a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sites/default/files/mcp-uploads/Homways-Chuzhou-12-inch-OLEDoS-fa", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/homways-formerly-metaways-starts-production-its-second-12-inch-oled", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-09-010", "date": "2026-11-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration", "mini_led"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "What OLED developers should know about microLED wearables: a new white paper details the status and roadmap", "content": "<p>If you are developing OLED displays or materials, it is worth following the progress of microLED - and especially in wearables, the first market in which the two technologies compete directly in a shipping consumer product. A new white paper from the <a href=\"https://www.microledassociation.com/\">MicroLED Industry Association</a> assesses the status of microLED wearable displays, the supply base and the roadmap to 2030. A summary edition is openly <a href=\"https://www.microledassociation.com/", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/what-oled-developers-should-know-about-microled-wearables-new-white-paper", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "csot-2026-11-09-011", "date": "2026-11-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": ["csot", "lg_elec", "tcl"], "customers": ["tcl"], "suppliers": ["csot"]}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["mass production"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["多公司提及", "供應鏈上下游同時提及"]}, "title": "Naintech to supply substrate transfer equipment for TCL CSOT's 8.6-Gen inkjet printed OLED line", "content": "<p>Korea-based equipment maker <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/naintech\">Naintech</a> announced that it will supply substrate transfer equipment for <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/csot-oled\">TCL CSOT</a>'s 8.6-Gen inkjet printed OLED mass production line in China. The equipment is supplied through LG Electronics, which signed a $18.7 million equipment supply contract with Naintech in June 2026.</p><p><img class=\"align-center\" src=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sites/default/files/mcp-uploads/", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/naintech-supply-substrate-transfer-equipment-tcl-csots-86-gen-inkjet-printed", "type": "rss"}]}
